---
title: Pigs in Blankets and White Bean Traybake
servings: 2
course: Main
locale: en
difficulty: Medium
---

Preheat the oven to 200°C.

Tip the undrained @cannellini beans{2%tins × 400 g}(undrained) into a large roasting tray. Add the @brussel sprouts{200%g}(finely sliced), @garlic{4%cloves}(grated), and the crumbled @chicken stock cube{1}. Drizzle 3 tbsp of @olive oil{4%tbsp} and fold everything together.

Wrap each @pork sausages{4} in a rasher of @streaky bacon{4%rashers}. Lay on top of the beans and drizzle with another 1 tbsp olive oil.

Bake for 20 to ~{25%minutes}, until the sausages are golden and cooked throughout. Meanwhile, soak the @dried cranberries{50%g} in boiling water.

Once the tray bake is ready, drain the cranberries, squeeze out any excess moisture, and scatter them over everything.